    "content" : "name: React Ace: Your React Journey Starts Now!\ndescription: Dive headfirst into the exciting world of React! React Ace is your ultimate guide to mastering the fundamentals of React, offering a fun and interactive learning experience. Test your knowledge with engaging quizzes, challenges, and real-world scenarios designed to solidify your understanding of components, JSX, state management, and more. Track your progress, compete with friends, and unlock achievements as you level up your React skills. Whether you're a complete beginner or looking to brush up on your basics, React Ace provides the perfect pathway to becoming a React pro. Get ready to build amazing web applications – download React Ace and start coding today!\n\n---question---\ntype: mcq\nquestion: What is JSX primarily used for in React?\noptions:\n1.  Handling server-side logic\n2.  Defining the structure and appearance of the user interface [correct]\n3.  Managing the state of components\n4.  Making HTTP requests\ntags: react, jsx, components\n\n---question---\ntype: true_false\nquestion: React Ace is only for experienced React developers.\ncorrect: false\ntags: react, beginners, learning\n\n---question---\ntype: written\nquestion: Explain the concept of \"components\" in React and why they are important.\ntags: react, components, architecture\n\n---question---\ntype: multi_select\nquestion: Which of the following are key concepts in React?\noptions:\n1.  Components [correct]\n2.  Variables\n3.  JSX [correct]\n4.  HTML\ntags: react, fundamentals, jsx, components\n"
  }
